      "writtenOn": "2023-10-11T01:13:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what happens when the first IOMMU  (in our case SMMU v2) calls iommu_device_register() without registering vendor hook. We attach this IOMMU to PCI bus as well. Then we end up calling bus_iommu_probe() and iterating over all PCI devices. \n\nThen when 2nd IOMMU (SMMU v3) registers now we override the PCI bus ops to 2nd IOMMU and iterate over all devices. \n\nI understand that it works. But that may break later. IMO, we should PCI bus_iommu_probe() it self from SMMU v2",
      "revId": "54b6cba3effd5a65350d2a2bb7f404eb048c1b17",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
